{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>For, etc.</b> The wonder is that every fortified city is captured while the place of the poor escapes, and this is Jerusalem, a refuge from a torrent, for the enemy is likened to water." "<b>For the wind of oppressors.</b> It explains \"from a torrent.\""], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:55:04.696190601Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}